# The offside rule
subtitle: "A player is offside only if she is past the last defender but one at the moment the ball is played, not when it arrives."
tags: ["football","soccer","offside","rules","sport"]
teaches: ["concepts/offside-rule"]
thumb: "band \"Offside or not?\" note \"it's all about timing\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Charon | a warm, clear teacher, quietly enjoying the idea"}

## The offside rule
setting: {"ground":"grass"}

    path pitch closed #5d7d50 points [[140,165],[850,165],[850,600],[140,600]] hidden true
    path box #5d7d50 points [[850,255],[720,255],[720,510],[850,510]] hidden true
    path goal thick #5d7d50 points [[850,345],[885,345],[885,420],[850,420]] hidden true
    ellipse att_sh #b5482e x 370 y 328 rx 30 ry 10 style.fill #b5482e style.fill_style wash style.opacity 0.55 hidden true
    icon att size 72 x 370 y 360 flip true icon_look picture of "person running" hidden true
    icon ball size 30 x 410 y 330 icon_look picture of "soccer ball" hidden true
    ellipse mate_sh #b5482e x 790 y 408 rx 30 ry 10 style.fill #b5482e style.fill_style wash style.opacity 0.55 hidden true
    icon mate size 72 x 790 y 440 flip true icon_look picture of "person running" hidden true
    ellipse def_sh #2f6b8f x 660 y 268 rx 30 ry 10 style.fill #2f6b8f style.fill_style wash style.opacity 0.55 hidden true
    icon def size 72 x 660 y 300 icon_look picture of "person standing" hidden true
    ellipse keeper_sh #2f6b8f x 815 y 348 rx 30 ry 10 style.fill #2f6b8f style.fill_style wash style.opacity 0.55 hidden true
    icon keeper size 72 x 815 y 380 icon_look picture of "person standing" hidden true
    path offline dashed #2f6b8f points [[660,165],[660,600]] hidden true
    text l_line "last defender but one" #2f6b8f x 660 y 622 font_size 22 hidden true
    text l_off "Offside" #b5482e x 790 y 520 hidden true
    text l_on "Onside" #4f7a3a x 560 y 520 hidden true
    arrow pass dashed #3d3833 from.x 425 from.y 352 to.x 765 to.y 455 hidden true

When is a footballer offside? Here the red team attacks to the right, toward the blue team's goal.
    draw pitch box goal

The red player on the ball wants to pass forward to her teammate, far up the pitch.
    draw att_sh att ball mate_sh mate

Between that teammate and the goal line stand two defenders: the keeper, and one more.
    draw def_sh def keeper_sh keeper

The rule watches the last defender but one. Picture a line across the pitch, level with him.
    draw offline l_line

If the teammate (@highlight mate@) is past that line when (@draw l_off@) the ball is played, she is offside, and the free kick goes to blue.

(@erase l_off@) So she (@move mate_sh mate by [-170,0] duration 1.2@) waits level with the line, or behind it.

Now she is onside, and the pass is fair.
    draw l_on

(@draw pass@) Once the ball is played she (@move mate_sh mate by [170,0] duration 1.4@) may sprint past the line to meet it.

Offside is judged at the moment of the pass, not when the ball arrives.
    text l_moment "judged at the pass" #3d3833 x 340 y 230

    quiz "She is level with the line when the ball is played, then sprints past it. Offside?"
        right: Not offside: only where she stood at the pass counts, and level is onside.
        * Yes: she ended up past the line
        + No: level at the pass is onside

So when the flag goes up, think back to the moment of the pass.
    highlight offline
